Unreleased (Rust Edition)
    * The Rust rewrite has not yet received a versioned release tag.
    * COMPLETE REWRITE IN RUST:
        * Significant performance improvements with repeatable benchmark reporting.
        * Memory-safe rendering using Rust idiomatic patterns.
        * Pure Cargo build system (legacy Makefiles removed).
    * NEW FEATURES:
        * TrueColor Support: Added -T/--truecolor flag for 24-bit HD rendering.
        * Benchmark Mode: Added -b/--benchmark flag with 0ms delay and key-value render stats.
    * OPTIMIZATIONS:
        * Enabled LTO and aggressive release optimizations.
        * Pre-computed ANSI color palettes for faster rendering.
    * MAY 2026:
        * Added --version, bounded crop and terminal dimensions, and improved 256-color detection.
        * Added NO_COLOR support for monochrome output.
        * Switched interactive sessions to the alternate screen and restored the terminal on more signals.
        * Fixed rendering at the right edge and when the terminal is resized.
    * JUNE 2026:
        * Telnet sessions now reflow the animation when the client window changes size.
        * Hardened the included systemd telnet service with security sandboxing.
    * JULY 2026:
        * Bounded remote telnet window reports and corrected unsupported-option negotiation.
        * Preserved genuine telnet I/O failures instead of reporting every disconnect as success.
        * Rejected unexpected positional arguments and invalid final crop ranges.
        * Restored terminal state on unwinding panics and preserved conventional signal status.
        * Made release publication wait for both platform artifacts and added SHA-256 checksums.
    * DOCUMENTATION:
        * Updated README.md, nyancat.1, release checklist, architecture notes, and benchmark snapshots.

